dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, carolyn, how are you?
[patient] hi, doc, i'm okay. i'm here for my follow-up.
[doctor] great. so, you know, i saw that you were here for a follow-up of your chronic problem. so, what's going on with your osteoarthritis? is it flaring up?
[patient] yeah, it has been flaring up a little bit lately, and i just wanted to talk about that. primarily in my elbows.
[doctor] okay. and what's going on with your elbows? which one is bothering you more?
[patient] my right elbow is bothering me more than my left.
[doctor] okay. and what have you been doing that's causing that?
[patient] i've been sitting at the computer more in the office, so i'm not sure if it's from sitting in that position all day.
[doctor] okay. so, are you sitting at the computer all day or are you doing other things?
[patient] i'm typing all day, so i'm not sure if that's causing it. i'm not writing, so i'm not using my left hand.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other joint pain?
[patient] no, just my elbows.
[doctor] okay. and then you mentioned some occasional numbness and tingling in your hands. how often is that?
[patient] occasionally.
[doctor] okay. and what do you do to relieve the numbness?
[patient] i try to shake out my arms.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other issues with your joints or anything else?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. and i know that you have a history of gout. how are you doing with that?
[patient] my last episode was about 3 months ago. i had some inflammation in my toe at that time.
[doctor] okay. and then have you had any other issues with that?
[patient] no, not really. the medication i was given helped with that, and i have not seen a flare up since.
[doctor] okay. and how about your psoriasis? how are you doing with that?
[patient] that's under control. it has not been a major problem for me.
[doctor] okay. and what medication are you taking for that?
[patient] i'm still on the colchicine.
[doctor] okay. and you take that twice a day as needed for flare-ups?
[patient] yes, that's right.
[doctor] okay. let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i'm gon na start with your neck. your neck is supple without any lymph nodes. on your respiratory exam, your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. on your cardiovascular exam, your heart rate and rhythm are regular. your abdomen is soft. and on your musculoskeletal exam, i don't see any edema of the lower extremities. now, let's look at your right elbow. i do see some edema and inflammation of the right olecranon. there is some tenderness to palpation of the olecranon bursa. pain with pronation and supination. pain with flexion and extension of your right arm. so, i'm gon na go ahead and order an x-ray of your right elbow. we'll also prescribe some meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day for the pain and swelling. and then we'll continue the colchicine 0.6 milligrams twice a day as needed for flare-ups of your gout. and you can continue with the steroid cream for your psoriasis. does that sound okay?
[patient] that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other questions?
[patient] no, that's it.
[doctor] okay. well, i'll have my nurse come in and get you checked out. thank you, carolyn.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
