dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, anna, how are you?
[patient] i'm okay, i'm just really struggling with some joint pain in my elbow.
[doctor] okay, so you're having some joint pain in your elbow. when did that start?
[patient] it started about a week ago.
[doctor] okay, and what has been going on with that?
[patient] it's really been bothering me. i sit at my desk all day at work and my elbows are bent. after work it's really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow. it's really stiff and painful. and i've noticed some swelling on the olecranon of my elbow.
[doctor] okay. and are you able to use your arm?
[patient] i'm right-handed, so i can still write, which is great, but typing is really difficult.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any numbness or tingling in your hands?
[patient] no, none of that.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any weakness in your arm?
[patient] there is some weakness, but nothing too significant.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any fever or chills?
[patient] no, none of that.
[doctor] okay. how about your epilepsy? how are you doing with that?
[patient] i haven't had any recent seizures. my last seizure was about a year ago.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking your medication?
[patient] yes, i'm still taking keppra.
[doctor] okay. and how about your depression? how are you doing with that?
[patient] i started therapy last year and i'm trying to avoid medications for this problem. therapy has been helpful, but i still feel down and stressed. but i haven't had any suicidal or homicidal ideations.
[doctor] okay. and how about your peptic ulcer? how are you doing with that?
[patient] i was dealing with a lot of stress last year. then i underwent an endoscopy and they found that i had an episode of gastritis. they diagnosed me with peptic ulcer disease and i started protonix. i have not had any issues with my ulcer since the procedure and everything has been good.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting?
[patient] no, i do have a little bit of medial nasal congestion from allergies.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no, none of that.
[doctor] okay. let's go ahead and do a physical exam. so on your physical exam, your vital signs are stable. your heart is regular, lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. your abdomen is soft and non-tender. your extremities are without edema or clubbing. on your musculoskeletal exam, there is erythema and edema of the left elbow. there is pain to palpation of the left olecranon. it's warm to palpation and painful with flexion and extension. there is a palpable left radial pulse. so i'm gon na order an x-ray of the left elbow. it did not reveal any evidence of an elbow fracture. your endoscopy revealed an episode of gastritis. so let's talk about your plan. for your left elbow pain, i believe you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma. i'm gon na initiate meloxicam 15 milligrams once daily. i want you to use a pillow to rest your arm on. you may also ice the area. for your epilepsy, you have been doing well on keppra. i want you to continue keppra 500 milligrams twice a day. i refilled it today. for your depression, you're doing well with therapy. i'm gon na initiate lexapro 10 milligrams once daily. and for your peptic ulcer disease, your recent endoscopy revealed gastritis. i want you to continue protonix 40 milligrams once daily before meals. do you have any questions?
[patient] no, i think that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. do you understand and agree with the recommended medical treatment plan?
[patient] yes, i understand and agree.
[doctor] great. do you have any other questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay. all right, thank you, anna. take care.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
