dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good afternoon, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay, i just need to get some tests done.
[doctor] alright, i'm doctor martin. i understand that you're here for full-spectrum std testing. what seems to be the reason for that?
[patient] yeah, so i've been having some symptoms and i'm just really worried about getting something.
[doctor] okay. so, what kind of symptoms are you experiencing?
[patient] um, discomfort, a change in my discharge, and a bad odor in my vaginal area.
[doctor] mm-hmm. and how long have you been noticing these symptoms?
[patient] it started about a week ago.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed anything else? like a fever or chills?
[patient] no, no fever or chills.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any pain in your lower abdomen or pelvis?
[patient] yes, the right side of my vagina is getting really painful and sore.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any changes in your discharge?
[patient] yeah, the color and the consistency is different.
[doctor] okay. and when you say the color and the consistency is different, what do you mean?
[patient] it's not normal. it's like it's thicker and it smells bad.
[doctor] okay. and how long have you been with your current partner?
[patient] we've been together for about three years.
[doctor] okay. and do you know if they've been with other people?
[patient] no, i just found out.
[doctor] okay. and did you find out recently?
[patient] yeah, recently. they told me.
[doctor] okay. and how did you find out?
[patient] they told me.
[doctor] okay. and how have you been feeling about this?
[patient] i'm really upset and worried.
[doctor] yeah, i can imagine. so, have you talked to them about it?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and have you talked to anyone else about it?
[patient] no, i just came here.
[doctor] okay. alright. well, i'm glad you're here. so, let's go ahead and do a quick exam. i'm just gon na do a pelvic exam. it's very quick and it's painless. i'm gon na just feel your abdomen and then i'm gon na look at your vagina. i'm just gon na check for any lesions or abnormalities. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] alright, i'm gon na just check your abdomen now. everything looks normal. i'm gon na check your vagina now. everything looks normal. i'm gon na check your cervix now. everything looks normal. your vaginal walls look normal. i don't see any cervical motion tenderness or any masses. i'm gon na get some swabs now to test for stds. we're gon na check for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. i know it's a lot, but we're gon na do all of them to make sure we catch everything. i know it's a lot to take in, but i'll be here to support you every step of the way. do you have any questions about the testing?
[patient] no, i think you covered everything.
[doctor] okay. great. we'll call you when we get the results. i'll have my nurse come in and we'll get you checked out. sound good?
[patient] yeah, that's fine.
[doctor] alright. i'm gon na go ahead and order the tests and we'll call you when we get the results. do you have any other questions?
[patient] no, that's all.
[doctor] okay. great. my nurse will be in shortly. do you have any other medical issues or concerns that we should know about?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. great. my nurse will be in shortly to get you checked out. do you have a primary care doctor?
[patient] i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. great. we'll get you set up with one if you need it. my nurse will be in shortly. thank you for coming in today.
[patient] thank you.
[doctor] okay. }}<|eot_id|>
