dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, how are you?
[patient] i'm okay. i've been having some stomach pain.
[doctor] okay, so you're having some stomach pain. can you tell me more about that?
[patient] yeah, it's been going on for about a week now. it's in the right side of my abdomen.
[doctor] okay. is it a sharp pain or a dull pain?
[patient] it's a dull pain.
[doctor] okay. and is it constant or does it come and go?
[patient] it's constant.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any nausea with it?
[patient] yes, i've been feeling nauseous.
[doctor] okay. and have you been vomiting?
[patient] no, i haven't been vomiting.
[doctor] okay. have you had any fevers?
[patient] i've had low-grade fevers.
[doctor] okay. and any chills?
[patient] no chills.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any changes in your bowel movements or any blood in your stool?
[patient] no, nothing like that.
[doctor] okay. have you had any changes in your appetite?
[patient] no, my appetite has been fine.
[doctor] okay. and any weight loss?
[patient] no, i haven't lost any weight.
[doctor] okay. all right. and have you had any recent travel or contact with anyone who's been sick?
[patient] no, i haven't traveled recently and nobody's been sick around me.
[doctor] okay. all right. have you had any history of gallstones?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay. have you had any other symptoms?
[patient] just the pain and nausea.
[doctor] okay. any other symptoms like vomiting or chills?
[patient] no, just the pain and nausea.
[doctor] okay. have you had any abdominal pain in the past?
[patient] yes, i had a gallbladder attack a few years ago and they did a lap cholecystectomy.
[doctor] okay. all right. have you had any other surgeries?
[patient] yes, i had a surgery for my gallbladder.
[doctor] okay. and how long ago was that?
[patient] a few years ago.
