dialogue is: {{ [doctor] Good morning, how are you today?

[patient] Good morning, I'm okay, thanks.

[doctor] Great. I see you're here for a follow-up today. How have you been doing since your last visit?

[patient] Not too bad, just a bit of a flare-up with my osteoarthritis.

[doctor] Hmm, sorry to hear that. Can you tell me more about what's been going on with your osteoarthritis?

[patient] Yes, it's been bothering me a bit lately. It's mainly in my elbows.

[doctor] Okay, which elbow is bothering you more?

[patient] My right elbow is bothering me more than my left one.

[doctor] Got it. Do you notice any specific activities or positions that make it worse?

[patient] I've been sitting at my computer at work a lot more lately, and I'm not sure if it's because I'm in the same position all day.

[doctor] That could definitely be a factor. Have you noticed any other joint pain besides your elbows?

[patient] No, just the elbows.

[doctor] And how about any numbness or tingling in your hands?

[patient] Yes, I get occasional numbness and tingling in my hands, but I just shake it out and it goes away.

[doctor] Alright. Have you had any issues with your gout recently?

[patient] Yes, I had an episode about 3 months ago. I had inflammation in my toe.

[doctor] I see. How did you treat that episode?

[patient] The medication I was given helped a lot, and I haven't had another flare-up since.

[doctor] Good to hear that. Are you still on colchicine for flare-ups?

[patient] Yes, I am. I take it 0.6 mg twice a day as needed.

[doctor] Okay, that's good. How about your psoriasis? Any issues with that?

[patient] No, my psoriasis has been under control. It hasn't been a big problem.

[doctor] That's good to hear. Any other issues you've noticed?

[patient] No, nothing else really.

[doctor] Alright. Let's do a quick review of your systems. How has your musculoskeletal system been?

[patient] My joints have been hurting a bit, especially my elbows.

[doctor] Okay. Any neurological issues?

[patient] I get occasional numbness and tingling in my hands.

[doctor] Alright. Let's do a physical exam. Your neck feels supple and there's no lymphadenopathy. Your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. Your heart sounds are regular and your abdomen is soft. I'll check your lower extremities and see if there's any swelling. There's no edema. Let's examine your right elbow. There is some edema and inflammation of the right olecranon. I'll check for tenderness. There is some tenderness to palpation of the olecranon bursa. You also have pain with pronation and supination, and pain with flexion and extension of your right arm.

[patient] Oh, that hurts.

[doctor] I'm sorry. I'll continue the exam. I'll order an x-ray of your right elbow to see if there's any joint damage. In the meantime, I'll prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once a day for pain and swelling. We'll also continue your colchicine for flare-ups of your gout. You're already on colchicine 0.6 mg twice a day as needed. Your psoriasis is under control, so we'll keep you on the steroid cream.

[patient] Alright, that sounds good. I'll start the meloxicam.

[doctor] Great. Do you have any questions about the treatment plan?

[patient] No, I think I understand everything.

[doctor] Good. You'll need to follow up in a few months to see how the treatment is working. We'll also need to do a follow-up on your right elbow x-ray. Do you have any other questions?

[patient] No, that's all.

[doctor] Alright. We'll see you in a few months. Take care and feel better.

[patient] Thank you, I will. Bye.

[doctor] Bye. }}<|eot_id|>
