[patient]: No, not there.

[doctor]: And in the right upper quadrant?

[patient]: No, none there either.

[doctor]: Alright, thank you. Based on your symptoms and exam, I think you're likely experiencing acute gastritis, possibly related to your increased caffeine intake and history of moderately heavy alcohol use.

[patient]: Oh, I see.

[doctor]: I’m going to recommend reducing your caffeine intake and alcohol. I’ll also prescribe you Zantac to help with your symptoms. Additionally, I’ll order a urinalysis, urine pregnancy test, CBC, and a comprehensive metabolic panel to rule out any other potential causes.

