[patient]: Okay, what’s the change?

[doctor]: I’m going to increase the morning dose to 1000 mg and keep the evening dose at 500 mg. It’s important to continue your home blood sugar monitoring and bring those readings to your next appointment.

[patient]: I’ll do that.

[doctor]: Good. Your asthma seems to be under control, but it’s important to continue taking your Flovent daily, even if you haven’t had any recent attacks. This will help decrease the frequency of your attacks. And continue using albuterol as needed.

[patient]: I’ll keep taking it.

[doctor]: Do you have any questions about the treatment plan?

[patient]: No, I think I understand.

[doctor]: Great. We’ll need to follow up in four weeks to check on your progress. Do you have any other questions or concerns?

[patient]: No, I think that’s it.

[doctor]: Alright, I’ll see you in four weeks. Take care.

