dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, carolyn, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i'm just a little bit frustrated with the elbow. it's been bothering me a lot lately.
[doctor] okay. tell me a little bit more about that. where is it bothering you?
[patient] well, i'm having a little bit of pain in my elbows. i'm not sure if it's from sitting at the computer all day, but it seems like it's been flaring up a little bit more lately.
[doctor] okay. and which elbow is bothering you more?
[patient] my right elbow.
[doctor] okay. and is that the one you're using more of? is that the one you're using more of or is it the left one?
[patient] i think it's probably the one i'm using more of because i'm typing on the computer, but i'm not sure if it's the right or left.
[doctor] okay. and is that the only joint that's bothering you or are you having pain in other joints as well?
[patient] no, just the elbows.
[doctor] okay. and are you having any other symptoms? like any numbness or tingling in your hands?
[patient] sometimes, yeah.
[doctor] okay. and how do you relieve that?
[patient] i just try to shake out my arms.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?
[patient] i have a history of gout.
[doctor] okay. and how often do you get gout?
[patient] i haven't had any gout in a while.
[doctor] okay. and what was the last episode of gout?
[patient] about three months ago.
[doctor] okay. and what was the location of the gout?
[patient] my toe.
[doctor] okay. and what did we do for the gout?
[patient] i was given some medication.
[doctor] okay. and what was the medication?
[patient] i'm not sure.
[doctor] okay. and what's been happening with your psoriasis?
[patient] i'm still having some psoriasis.
[doctor] okay. and are you having any flare-ups of that?
[patient] no, it's under control.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. all right, so i'm gon na go ahead and do a quick physical exam on you. so your neck is supple without any lymph nodes. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. your heart is regular rate and rhythm. your abdomen is soft. and your lower extremities are clear of any edema. your right elbow, i do appreciate some edema and inflammation of the right olecranon. some tenderness to palpation of the olecranon bursa. pain with pronation and supination of the right arm, and pain with flexion and extension of the right arm. so i'm gon na go ahead and order an x-ray of the right elbow. and i'm gon na prescribe meloxicam fifteen milligrams once a day for the pain and swelling in your elbow. and i'm gon na continue you on the colchicine. i'm gon na prescribe that you take that once a day as needed for flare-ups of your gout. and i'm gon na continue you on the steroid cream for your psoriasis. and i'm gon na go ahead and send you a prescription for that. do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. all right, i'll get my nurse to come in and get you checked out and get you set up with that prescription. is there anything else you'd like to talk about?
[patient] no, that's it.
[doctor] okay, all right. well, i'll see you soon.
[patient] okay, thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
