dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey anna how are you
[patient] i'm doing okay
[doctor] all right good to see you so i know that you're here today for some joint pain i know you said it's in your left elbow so tell me a little bit more about that
[patient] okay so i sit at my desk all day for work and i'm always bending my elbows so it's just been really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow after work it's just really stiff and painful and i've noticed some swelling on the olecranon of my elbow
[doctor] okay
[patient] and i'm right handed so i can still write which is great but typing is really difficult and i've also noticed some weakness in my arm but nothing too significant and i haven't had any numbness or tingling in my hands
[doctor] okay and have you had any fever or chills
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and how about any chest pain shortness of breath abdominal pain nausea or vomiting
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and how about any depression or anxiety
[patient] i've been feeling down and stressed a lot lately but i'm still trying to avoid medication for that i started therapy last year and that's been helpful but i still feel down and stressed but i haven't had any suicidal or homicidal ideations
[doctor] okay and have you been having any seizures
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and how about any chest pain or shortness of breath
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and have you been having any abdominal pain or nausea or vomiting
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and any nasal congestion
[patient] i do have a little bit of medial nasal congestion from allergies
[doctor] okay all right so let's do a quick physical exam i'm just gon na look in your ears and your throat okay
[patient] okay
[doctor] and your ears and your throat look good and now i'm gon na listen to your heart and lungs okay
[patient] okay
[doctor] and everything sounds good on that side now i'm gon na do a quick examination of your left elbow okay
[patient] okay
[doctor] so there is some erythema and edema i don't feel any heat but there is some pain to palpation of the olecranon and it is painful to flex and extend and i do feel a palpable left radial pulse
[patient] okay
[doctor] all right now i'm gon na look at your x-ray and it doesn't show any evidence of elbow fracture and i'm gon na look at your endoscopy and it shows that you had an episode of gastritis so let's talk about your joint pain so i think you have olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma from sitting at your desk all day so i'm gon na start you on meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day and i want you to use a pillow to rest your arm on and you can also ice the area and i want to continue you on that for a few weeks and see how you do and if that doesn't get better we may need to do a cortisone injection so for your epilepsy i know you have been doing well on keppra and i'm gon na continue you on that 500 milligrams twice a day and for your depression i'm gon na start you on lexapro 10 milligrams once a day and i want you to continue therapy and i'm gon na continue you on protonix 40 milligrams once a day before meals for your peptic ulcer disease so i know that you've been doing well on that so let's do a quick review of your system okay
[patient] okay
[doctor] so in terms of your ears nose and throat you do have some medial nasal congestion from allergies in terms of your cardiovascular system you don't have any chest pain or dyspnea on exertion in terms of your respiratory system you don't have any shortness of breath and in terms of your musculoskeletal system you do have left elbow joint pain and swelling and weakness and in terms of your psychiatric system you do have depression and your last seizure was a year ago so i'm gon na go ahead and refill your keppra and i'm gon na see you in three weeks and we can recheck the joint and see if you need any further treatment so any questions for me
[patient] no that's fine thank you
[doctor] okay }}<|eot_id|>
