dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, susan.
[patient] hi.
[doctor] how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well, thank you.
[doctor] so, i know that you've been having some high blood pressure. is that correct?
[patient] yes, i have high blood pressure.
[doctor] okay. and when was that diagnosed?
[patient] it's been a long time. i don't remember.
[doctor] okay.
[patient] i've always had high blood pressure.
[doctor] okay. and is it out of control?
[patient] it seems out of control.
[doctor] okay. have you been taking any medications for it?
[patient] i've been taking norvasc ten milligrams daily.
[doctor] okay. and is that helping?
[patient] i'm not sure.
[doctor] okay. have you been checking your blood pressure at home?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and what's been your blood pressure?
[patient] it's been over one fifty.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any chest pain or shortness of breath?
[patient] no, i have had some headaches.
[doctor] okay. and is that from stress at work or is it from your blood pressure?
[patient] i'm not sure.
[doctor] okay. and have you been taking your norvasc?
[patient] i've been taking it.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, i'm gon na go ahead and check your blood pressure. and i'm gon na listen to your heart. and i'm gon na do a quick physical exam. and then we'll go ahead and discuss some treatment options.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay, so your blood pressure is a little elevated today, which is a good thing because we can check it. and on your physical exam, your heart is regular rate and rhythm, and there's a little bit of a systolic ejection murmur that's normal. and on your lungs, they're clear to auscultation bilaterally. no wheezes, rales or rhonchi. and on your abdomen, there's a scar from your kidney transplant, which is good. and on your skin, there's no edema. all in all, you look good.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so, i'd like to order a lipid panel and a metabolic panel.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'd like to start you on carvedilol twenty-five milligrams twice a day.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'd like you to continue your norvasc ten milligrams daily. and i'd like you to come back in a month to check your blood pressure again. and we'll go from there.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and how are you doing otherwise?
[patient] i'm doing well.
[doctor] okay. and i know you've had a kidney transplant a few years ago. how's that going?
[patient] it's going well.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking your immunosuppression medications?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. and is everything stable?
[patient] yes, it is.
[doctor] okay. good. and are you having any side effects from those medications?
[patient] no, i'm not.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, i'm glad to hear that. and i'm gon na go ahead and order some lab tests. and i'll see you back in a month.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay?
[patient] thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
