dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi there, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i've been having some back pain.
[doctor] okay. so tell me a little bit more about what happened. how did you hurt your back?
[patient] i was at a birthday party and i ran my back into the railing of the staircase and twisted my back.
[doctor] okay. and how are you feeling now?
[patient] i'm feeling pretty sore. it hurts when i lie flat and twist my back.
[doctor] okay. and do you feel pain radiating down your legs?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. have you tried any treatment so far?
[patient] i've just been taking ibuprofen.
[doctor] okay. all right. i'm going to go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i'm just going to check your back. how's your back doing?
[patient] it's sore.
[doctor] okay. so i'm going to go ahead and do a quick exam. and i'm just going to check your reflexes and sensation in your legs. so your reflexes are normal, and your sensation is intact. and your back does seem to have a little bit of limitation in terms of flexion and extension. but it does seem to be stable. i'm also going to go ahead and take a look at your x-rays. so your x-rays of your back show no obvious signs of an acute fracture, and you do have a prior lumbar fusion, and that fusion appears to be in good position. and i can see the hardware is intact. so i'm going to go ahead and give you a diagnosis of lumbar spine strain. and i'm just going to recommend a few things for you to do. i'm going to recommend that you take ibuprofen 800 mg three times a day with food. and i want you to stay off of work for a few days. and i want you to use ice and heat. you can start with ice for the first couple of days and then switch to heat. and if your symptoms do not get better, then we can go ahead and discuss other treatment options. i'm going to go ahead and prescribe you a few days of physical therapy. and if you're still having problems, we can discuss other surgical options. but i think at this point, i think you're going to be okay. is that okay with you?
[patient] that sounds good. thank you.
[doctor] okay. do you have any questions?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. i'm going to go ahead and go ahead and go ahead and give you a prescription for the physical therapy. and i'm also going to go ahead and give you a prescription for the ibuprofen. i'm going to go ahead and go ahead and order the physical therapy and the ibuprofen. and if you have any other questions, feel free to call me. i'm going to go ahead and go ahead and go ahead and go ahead and get you checked out.
[patient] okay. thank you.
[doctor] okay. bye bye.
[patient] bye bye. }}<|eot_id|>
