dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, ms. thompson. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well. how are you?
[doctor] i'm doing well. so, i know you were here a couple of years ago for your carpal tunnel release. and i know you had some back pain. and i know you've been doing really well with that. but, i know you've been a little more active lately. and i know you've been swimming a lot. and i know you've been doing some other activities, like hiking and stuff. and you've been doing well with that. but, i know you've been having some pain in your knee. and i was wondering if we could talk about that a little bit today. how's your back been?
[patient] my back has been doing really well. it's been doing well.
[doctor] good. and how's your depression been?
[patient] it's been going really well. i've been getting outside a lot and that's been helping me a lot with my depression.
[doctor] that's great. i'm glad to hear that. so, let's talk about your knee a little bit. how long have you been having this pain?
[patient] it's been about a month.
[doctor] okay. and what type of activities are you doing that make the pain worse?
[patient] um, swimming.
[doctor] okay. and how long have you been doing that?
[patient] um, i've been doing that for a couple of months now.
[doctor] okay. and what type of swimming are you doing?
[patient] um, just freestyle.
[doctor] okay. and how many laps do you normally do?
[patient] um, ten.
[doctor] okay. and when you started doing this, did you notice the pain right away?
[patient] no, i didn't. i think it started after a couple of laps.
[doctor] okay. and how many laps would you say you're doing now?
[patient] um, probably about five.
[doctor] okay. and do you feel like it's getting better or worse?
[patient] it's getting worse.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any pain in your back?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and any pain in your leg?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any numbness or tingling in your leg?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. do you have any pain in your ankle?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. do you have any pain in your foot?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. have you injured your knee at all?
[patient] no.
