dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, jordan how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay.
[doctor] good. so, you know, i know we've been following you for a while, and we've been trying to get your blood pressure under control. how's everything going?
[patient] well, i've been doing pretty good. i've been watching my diet, and i've been walking a lot.
[doctor] okay. well, i know you've been taking some of your medications, and i know you've been feeling good. but i know you've had some palpitations, and i know you've been feeling some high blood pressure. so i want to talk to you a little bit about that. tell me, have you had any palpitations?
[patient] yeah, i've had a couple of times where my heart has been racing.
[doctor] okay. and when did this happen?
[patient] about a month ago.
[doctor] okay. and what did you do?
[patient] i went to the emergency room.
[doctor] okay. and what did they say?
[patient] they said it was a panic attack.
[doctor] okay. and did they give you anything?
[patient] no, they didn't give me anything.
[doctor] okay. and did you take anything?
[patient] i think i took some ibuprofen.
[doctor] okay. and did you have any other symptoms?
[patient] no, i was just really nervous.
[doctor] okay. and how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing okay.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any palpitations now?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. so, i know that you've been monitoring your blood pressure at home, and i know you've been getting readings of about 146 to 155. is that correct?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay. have you been monitoring your blood pressure for a while?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay. and how long has that been?
[patient] for about a month.
[doctor] okay. and have you been watching your diet? have you been watching your salt intake?
[patient] yeah, i have been watching my diet. i've been trying to cut back on salt.
[doctor] okay. and how much salt are you consuming a day?
[patient] i'm not sure. i try to keep it low.
[doctor] okay. well, i think you should try to get it under 2000 milligrams a day.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and what about your family history? do you have a family history of high blood pressure?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking any medications?
[patient] i'm taking amlodipine and benicar.
[doctor] okay. and how long have you been taking those for?
[patient] for a while.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any side effects?
[patient] no, not that i can think of.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na go ahead and listen to your heart. your heart is nice and regular. i'm gon na listen to your lungs. your lungs sound clear. i'm gon na listen to your abdomen. your abdomen is nice and soft. i'm gon na check your pulses. your pulses are nice and strong. i'm gon na check your reflexes. your reflexes are normal. so, let's talk a little bit about your blood pressure. i know you've been monitoring your blood pressure at home. you've been getting readings of 146 to 155. is that correct?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay. and how long have you been getting those readings?
[patient] for about a month.
[doctor] okay. and have you been taking your medications regularly?
[patient] yeah, i've been taking them every day.
[doctor] okay. and have you been watching your diet?
[patient] yeah, i've been watching my diet.
[doctor] okay. well, i think we need to make some adjustments. so, i'm gon na add spironolactone to your regimen. i'm gon na have you start that today. we're gon na monitor your potassium and sodium. i'm gon na have you come back in two weeks. i'm gon na check your blood pressure again, and i'm gon na check your basic metabolic panel. and if your blood pressure is still high, i'm gon na add carvedilol. so, let's talk a little bit about spironolactone. spironolactone is a medication that can help lower your blood pressure. it's a pill that you take once a day. it can cause some side effects. some of the side effects are gynecomastia, which means you'll develop breast tissue in your chest. it can cause some electrolyte disturbances, like potassium and sodium disturbances. it can cause you to retain water. so, if you start to feel dizzy, you need to come in and see me right away. i want you to monitor your blood pressure daily. i want you to take your blood pressure every morning and every evening. i want you to monitor your sodium intake. i want you to try to get it under 2000 milligrams a day. i want you to follow the dash diet. i'm gon na give you some materials. i want you to try to walk at least thirty minutes a day. i know you've been walking on your treadmill. i want you to walk at least thirty minutes a day. i want you to come back in two weeks. we'll check your blood pressure again. we'll check your basic metabolic panel. and if your blood pressure is still high, i'm gon na add carvedilol. so, let's talk a little bit about carvedilol. carvedilol is a medication that can also help lower your blood pressure. it's a pill that you take once a day. it can cause some side effects. some of the side effects are dizziness, drowsiness, and nausea. so, let's talk a little bit about some of the websites that we can look at. i want you to go to heart.org. that's the american heart association. i want you to look at some of the tips on lowering your salt intake and increasing your potassium intake. i want you to reduce your salt intake to 1500 to less than 2000 milligrams a day. i want you to follow the dash diet. i want you to meet thirty minutes of walking most days. so, let's talk a little bit about the next steps. i'm gon na have you come back in two weeks. we'll check your blood pressure again. we'll check your basic metabolic panel. if your blood pressure is still high, i'm gon na add carvedilol. so, any questions?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. good. i'm gon na go ahead and order some spironolactone for you. i'm gon na order some carvedilol for you. i'm gon na have my nurse call in the prescription to your pharmacy. i want you to call me back in two weeks. i want you to come in and see me. i want you to bring your blood pressure readings. i want you to bring your basic metabolic panel. we'll check your blood pressure again. we'll check your basic metabolic panel again. and if your blood pressure is still high, i'm gon na add carvedilol. so, i'm gon na go ahead and order some spironolactone. i'm gon na have my nurse call in the prescription to your pharmacy. i want you to call me back in two weeks. i want you to come in and see me. i want you to bring your blood pressure readings. i want you to bring your basic metabolic panel. we'll check your blood pressure again. we'll check your basic metabolic panel again. and if your blood pressure is still high, i'm gon na add carvedilol. }}<|eot_id|>
