dialogue is: {{ [doctor] so christopher watson is an eighty six year old male who returns in follow up of adult hydrocephalus this is his first visit since undergoing shunt surgery on august first twenty twenty he is accompanied by his daughter theresa together they give his history
[patient] my name is christopher watson i'm eighty six years old
[doctor] and your daughter is theresa
[patient] yes
[doctor] so i've followed you since may twenty twenty you presented with eight to ten years of progressive gait impairment cognitive impairment and decreased bladder control we established a diagnosis of adult hydrocephalus with the spinal catheter protocol in june twenty twenty and you underwent shunt surgery on august first twenty twenty a medtronic strata programmable shunt in the ventriculoperitoneal configuration programmed at level two point zero was placed
[patient] okay
[doctor] so you've had no hospitalizations or other illnesses since i last saw you with respect to your walking your daughter says that you are now able to walk to the dining room just fine but could not before your surgery your balance has improved though you still have some walking impairment with respect to your bladder control initially there was some improvement but you have leveled off and you wear a diaper with respect to your cognition both theresa and the patient say that your thinking has improved the other daughter hannah summarized it best according to the two of them she said i feel like i can have a normal conversation with him again you've had no headaches and no pain at the shunt site or in the abdomen
[patient] no
[doctor] so let's talk a little bit about your past history do you have a history of urinary incontinence
[patient] yes i do
[doctor] okay and you had adult hydrocephalus and gait impairment and cognitive impairment
[patient] yes
