[patient] no
[doctor] any unintentional weight loss
[patient] no
[doctor] any genitourinary problems
[patient] no
[doctor] any headaches
[patient] no
[doctor] any recent falls
[patient] no
[doctor] any hallucinations
[patient] no
[doctor] any depression
[patient] no
[doctor] any excessive worrying or mood swings
[patient] no
[doctor] okay so let's talk a little bit about your vital signs your blood pressure is one twenty four over eighty your heart rate is sixty four your respiratory rate is eighteen your weight is one seventy four pounds and your pain is zero out of ten
[patient] okay
[doctor] so let's talk a little bit about your physical exam your constitutional exam is normal your head and face exam is normal the shunt site is clean dry and intact and confirmed at a setting of two point zero your neurological exam is as follows your mental status is intact your memory is intact your attention span is intact your fund of knowledge is intact your gait is intact with a score of six to eight out of twelve and a balance of twelve out of sixteen for a total score of eighteen to twenty out of twenty eight which is slightly improved from your initial score of fifteen to seventeen out of twenty eight your cranial nerves are intact your motor exam is normal for bulk and strength and your coordination is slow for finger to nose
[patient] okay
[doctor] so let's talk a little bit about the results of your ct scan of the head from october fifteenth twenty twenty it shows a frontal horn span at the level of foramen of munro of four point six centimeters with a third ventricular contour that is flat with the span of ten millimeters by my reading there is a tiny amount of blood in the right frontal region with just a tiny subdural collection this was not noticed by the radiologist who stated no extra axial fluid collections there is also substantial small vessel ischemic change
