[doctor] so i think that you've made some progress with your hydrocephalus i do not believe that you will be able to drive again i think it is unlikely that your speed of movement will improve to a level that you will be able to pass a driver's safety evaluation however occasionally patients surprise me by improving enough over nine to twelve months that they are able to pass such a test i would certainly be happy to recommend such a test if i believe you are likely to pass it and you are always welcome to enroll in a driver's safety program without my recommendation however i think it is exceeding unlikely that you have the capability of passing this rigorous test
[patient] okay
[doctor] so i had a long discussion with the patient and his daughter we are all pleased that you have started to make some improvement with your hydrocephalus because of the fluid collection in the right parietal region i would like to leave the setting at two point zero for another three months before we consider changing the shunt
