dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, matthew. how are you doing?
[patient] i'm doing good.
[doctor] good. so, i'm matthew allen. i'm a 67-year-old male, right-hand-dominant male who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of a right shoulder injury.
[patient] mm-hmm.
[doctor] so, how did this injury occur?
[patient] i was playing football, and i was tackled a couple of times and i landed on my right shoulder.
[doctor] okay. and were you able to continue playing?
[patient] i was able to continue playing.
[doctor] okay. and how long ago did that happen?
[patient] it was about four days ago.
[doctor] okay. and since then, have you been able to continue playing football?
[patient] no, i haven't been able to continue playing.
[doctor] okay. and what have you been doing for pain?
[patient] i've been taking tylenol.
[doctor] okay. and how have you been doing?
[patient] i've been doing okay. i've been trying to avoid lifting anything too heavy, but i'm able to move my arm.
[doctor] okay. and what about your right shoulder? where is your pain located?
[patient] it's located on the back of my shoulder.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any numbness or tingling in your fingers?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. and how about your strength in your hand?
[patient] it's okay. i've been trying to avoid lifting anything too heavy.
[doctor] okay. and can you touch your ear to your shoulder?
[patient] no, i can't.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any neck problems or other joint problems?
[patient] no, i do not.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any previous injuries to your right shoulder?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any fever or chills?
[patient] no, i do not.
[doctor] okay. and how about a headache?
[patient] i have had a headache.
[doctor] okay. and did you hit your head?
[patient] yes, i hit my head.
[doctor] okay. and did you pass out?
[patient] no, i did not.
[doctor] okay. good. so, let's do a quick physical exam. so, on your neck, i'm just going to press on the back of your neck here. how does that feel?
[patient] it feels good.
[doctor] okay. and on your head, i'm just going to examine that. there does not appear to be any trauma. no ecchymosis or bruising. and on your right shoulder, i'm just going to press on the back of your shoulder. how does that feel?
[patient] it hurts.
[doctor] okay. and if i move your arm up and down, is that painful?
[patient] yes, it is.
[doctor] okay. and if i move your arm across your body, is that painful?
[patient] yes, it is.
[doctor] okay. and if i rotate your arm, is that painful?
[patient] yes, it is.
[doctor] okay. and if i press on your elbow, is that painful?
[patient] it's a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and if i press on your wrist, is that painful?
[patient] no, it is not.
[doctor] okay. and i'm just going to feel your radial pulse here. can you feel that?
[patient] yes, i can.
[doctor] okay. good. so, i'm gon na go ahead and review your x-rays now. so, the x-ray of your right shoulder reveals an acute acromioclavicular joint fracture. so, i'm gon na have a discussion with you about that now. so, i know you were playing football and you were tackled a couple of times and landed on your right shoulder. and since then, you've been having some pain. so, i know that you have an x-ray of your right shoulder that shows an acute acromioclavicular joint fracture. so, i'm gon na go ahead and show you the x-ray now. so, on this x-ray, you can see that the acromion and the clavicle are not aligned, which is consistent with an acromioclavicular joint fracture. so, i'm gon na have a discussion with you about the treatment options for that now. so, i'm gon na prescribe you some meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day to help with the pain. i'm gon na also recommend that we get a ct scan of your right shoulder to evaluate further. and i'm gon na recommend that you attend formal physical therapy to strengthen your right shoulder in hopes of avoiding surgery in the future. and in the meantime, i'm gon na advise you to avoid tackle football. is that okay?
[patient] that's fine.
[doctor] okay. do you have any questions?
[patient] no, i do not.
[doctor] okay. good. well, i'm gon na go ahead and order the meloxicam and the ct scan for you today. and we'll have our nurse come in and get you set up for that. and then i'm gon na have the physical therapist come in and we can discuss further physical therapy. is that okay?
[patient] yes, that's fine.
[doctor] okay. great. well, i'll see you in a little bit. thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
