dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, gregory. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well. how are you?
[doctor] good. so gregory, you're here today for the evaluation of a right knee injury. so tell me a little bit about what happened.
[patient] well, i stepped off of a curb and i turned over my ankle and i fell down.
[doctor] okay. and where do you feel the pain?
[patient] it's on the outside of my knee.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any pain with ambulation?
[patient] i do, but it's not all the time. only when i'm standing on one foot for a long time.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any pain when you're standing?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and any pain when you're elevated?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and when you're flat on the ground?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and any pain with locking of the knee?
[patient] yes, when i stand for a long time.
[doctor] okay. and do you feel any pain when you're resting your foot on your heel?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and do you feel any pain at rest?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and any pain when you're on one foot for a long time?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and do you feel any numbness and tingling in your right foot?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and is this new?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any similar injuries in the past?
[patient] no, not like this.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any medical problems?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any surgeries?
[patient] i had surgery on my ankle.
[doctor] okay. and when was that?
[patient] about 10 years ago.
[doctor] okay. and what was the diagnosis?
[patient] i broke my second toe.
[doctor] okay. and how many times did you break your second toe?
[patient] three times.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other surgeries?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and what kind of work do you do?
[patient] sales.
[doctor] okay. and do you have a regular exercise routine?
[patient] yes, i ride a bike.
[doctor] okay. and what's your occupation?
[patient] sales.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any allergies to any medications?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and what have you been doing for your pain?
[patient] i've been taking ibuprofen and i've been icing it.
[doctor] okay. and how many times a day are you icing it?
[patient] four times a day.
[doctor] okay. and how many times a day are you taking ibuprofen?
[patient] i'm not sure.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other injuries?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and any other surgeries?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any other injuries?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. all right. so gregory, i'm gon na go ahead and examine you. and i'm gon na go ahead and listen to your heart and lungs. and i'm gon na check your vital signs. and i'm gon na go ahead and do a physical exam of your right knee. and i'm gon na go ahead and do a neurovascular exam of your right leg.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. so on physical exam of your right knee, i do appreciate some edema and some effusion. and i do appreciate some pain with palpation of the right lateral knee. and i do appreciate some pain with varus testing. and i do appreciate full range of motion. and i do appreciate a negative lachman's test.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. and on my review of systems, i do appreciate some numbness and tingling in your right foot from prior injury.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. and looking at your radiographs, i do appreciate some bony edema, but i do not appreciate any fractures or dislocations or bony abnormalities. and i do appreciate no other abnormalities.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. so gregory, i'm gon na go ahead and tell you what i found. so i think you have a right knee lateral collateral ligament strain. and i think this is from your recent injury. and i think it's likely from your injury when you stepped off of the curb. and i think that this is something that we can treat conservatively with formal physical therapy. and i'm gon na go ahead and prescribe you meloxicam 15 milligrams. and i want you to take this 2 times a day. and i want you to take this for 7 to 10 days. and i want you to follow up with me in a week. and if you do not have any improvement in your pain, i'm gon na go ahead and recommend that we get an mri of your knee.
[patient] okay. is that going to help with the pain?
[doctor] yes, it should help with your pain. and i want you to go ahead and start physical therapy today. and i want you to go 2 times a week for 2 weeks. and i want you to do the exercises that the physical therapist gives you. and i want you to do this 2 times a day. and i want you to continue taking the meloxicam 15 milligrams 2 times a day. and i want you to follow up with me in a week. and if you do not have any improvement in your pain, i'm gon na go ahead and recommend that we get an mri of your knee.
[patient] okay. thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
