dialogue is: {{ [doctor] dennis martin is a pleasant 46-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of right heel pain. he is a triathlete who started his training for a triathlon about a month ago. the onset of his pain began about 10 days ago. he says it is the posterior aspect of his heel that is painful. it radiates proximally into his calf. his pain is aggravated by working out and when he first gets up in the morning. if he sits for a long period, his pain will return upon standing. he says he runs 10 kilometers in the morning. at lunchtime, he tries to get on a bike for about 45 minutes to an hour. in the evening, he goes to the aquatic center and swims for 30 minutes to an hour. the patient states that he runs 5 days per week. he adds that he alternates between a long run and a long bike ride on weekends. he currently takes one day off from his exercises. he states that he does not stretch at all. he denies any left leg pain.

[doctor] so dennis, i know you're a triathlete. i know you're trying to get ready for a triathlon. how are you doing with your training so far?
[patient] yeah, i'm doing pretty well. i've been training for about a month now.
[doctor] okay. and you're doing well. so you're doing a lot of running, biking, and swimming. and you've been doing that for a month now?
[patient] yeah, i have. i've been doing a lot of long runs. i've been running about 10 kilometers in the morning, and then i'll try to get on a bike for about 45 minutes to an hour. and then i go to the aquatic center and swim for 30 minutes to an hour. and then i'll do the same thing in the evening. i'm trying to do it five days a week.
[doctor] okay. and you're taking a day off?
[patient] yeah, i'm trying to take one day off a week.
[doctor] okay. and you're doing that for a month now?
[patient] yeah, i have.
[doctor] okay. and you said you're doing well, but you're having some pain in your right heel?
[patient] yeah, i am.
[doctor] okay. so tell me about that. where is the pain?
[patient] it's on the back of my heel.
[doctor] okay. and does it radiate up into your calf?
[patient] yeah, it does.
[doctor] okay. and does it hurt when you get up in the morning?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and how about when you're sitting for a long time? does it hurt when you get up?
[patient] yeah, it does.
[doctor] okay. and when you're working out, does it hurt?
[patient] yeah, it does.
[doctor] okay. and when you're running, does it hurt?
[patient] yeah, it does.
[doctor] okay. and when you're biking, does it hurt?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and when you're swimming, does it hurt?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and does it hurt on your left side?
[patient] no.
