[patient] it's a little bit sore, but i've been able to move it.
[doctor] okay. and is it swollen at all?
[patient] a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and any bruising?
[patient] yeah, a little bit of bruising.
[doctor] okay. um, and do you have any history of any other injuries to your elbow?
[patient] no, not that i can think of.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any history of any other medical problems?
[patient] i'm a type two diabetic and i have high blood pressure.
[doctor] okay. okay. and how long have you had diabetes?
[patient] i've had it for about ten years.
[doctor] okay. and how long have you had high blood pressure?
[patient] i've had it for a long time, i'm not sure.
[doctor] okay. and are you currently on any medications for that?
[patient] yes, i'm on lisinopril.
[doctor] okay. and how much of that do you take?
[patient] twenty milligrams a day.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking it in the morning or at night?
[patient] in the morning.
[doctor] okay. and have you been taking it as prescribed?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay. and are you watching your diet?
[patient] yes, i'm watching my diet.
[doctor] okay. and how much weight have you lost recently?
[patient] not much, not much.
[doctor] okay. and how much weight do you need to lose?
[patient] probably ten pounds.
[doctor] okay. um, have you had a hemoglobin a1c done recently?
[patient] yes, i had one a few weeks ago.
[doctor] okay. and what was that number?
[patient] it was six point nine.
[doctor] okay. and is that within a normal range?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. um, and are you on any other medications for your diabetes?
[patient] yes, i'm on metformin.
[doctor] okay. how much of that do you take?
[patient] five hundred milligrams a day.
[doctor] okay. and when do you take that?
[patient] in the morning and at night.
[doctor] okay. and how long have you been on that?
[patient] a few years.
[doctor] okay. um, and have you been able to control your blood sugar?
[patient] yes, i have.
[doctor] okay. okay. well, um, i'm going to go ahead and check your blood pressure. so, your blood pressure is one fifty over ninety. that's a little bit high, so i'm going to put you on a diet and i'm going to increase your lisinopril to twenty-five milligrams a day.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and we'll see you in three months. um, let's go ahead and get an x-ray of your elbow. i'm going to go ahead and order that for you. um, in the meantime, i want you to stay off of the lacrosse stick, so i don't want you playing for the next couple of weeks. and then you can start playing again after that. um, i'm also going to prescribe you some ibuprofen eight hundred milligrams twice a day, and i want you to ice the area for twenty minutes three times a day to help with the swelling.
